479
00:36:06,660 --> 00:36:12,640
The chemistry lab primarily relies upon three different types of instrumentation.

480
00:36:13,180 --> 00:36:20,320
One type is known as spectrophotometry, which basically is looking at how chemicals absorb or emit light.

481
00:36:20,321 --> 00:36:29,400
The second type are chromatic instruments, things that will take a complex mixture and separate them into their individual components.

482
00:36:30,280 --> 00:36:34,600
And then the high-end instrumentation is what's known as mass spectrometry.

483
00:36:34,601 --> 00:36:48,063
These are instruments that allow us to look at a chemical's fingerprint or its weight and combine that information to say with 100% certainty that a chemical is this

484
00:36:48,064 --> 00:36:49,940
and not something else.

485
00:36:50,320 --> 00:36:58,320
Perhaps the most advanced instrument in the chem lab's impressive arsenal is the time-of-flight mass spectrometer.

486
00:36:58,321 --> 00:37:07,320
Well, time-of-flight is, as the name suggests, it's actually measuring the amount of time that it takes a chemical to travel down a particular tube.

487
00:37:07,321 --> 00:37:16,320
Now, we're talking microseconds, but chemicals of different sizes and different configurations are going to do so at different speeds.

488
00:37:16,321 --> 00:37:22,320
This is because all chemicals have distinct atomic weights, which affects their speed of travel.

489
00:37:22,321 --> 00:37:29,320
The lighter elements pass down the tube more quickly, thus reaching the detector in a shorter amount of time.

490
00:37:29,321 --> 00:37:37,320
What the time-of-flight mass spectrometers allow us to do is look at chemicals and their weights with high resolution.

491
00:37:37,321 --> 00:37:43,020
For example, if I were to look at an individual and say that they weigh 180 pounds,

492
00:37:43,160 --> 00:37:47,220
that would be the equivalent of what I can do with older type mass spectrometers.

493
00:37:47,560 --> 00:37:52,980
But now, with the introduction of the time-of-flight mass spectrometers and their high resolution,

494
00:37:52,981 --> 00:38:00,220
I can now look at an individual and say that their weight is 180.5749 pounds.

495
00:38:01,500 --> 00:38:04,980
This instrument enables a microscopic level of certainty

496
00:38:04,981 --> 00:38:09,660
in identifying compounds and elements that was previously not even dreamt of.

497
00:38:10,600 --> 00:38:15,740
But while the chemistry and trace evidence units have evolved slowly but constantly over the years,

